  "query_preview": "..The unprecedented east wind event with widely\nscattered gusts between 55 and 80 mph continues this morning. \nTucson airport recorded its highest wind gust for this event of \n66 mph at 115 am. Mt. Hopkins (7120' Santa Rita Mtns) continues\nto see the highest gusts of 70+ mph. Yesterday Mt Hopkins 24 \nhour average was 38 mph sustained and 63 mph gusts. Tucson \nyesterday unofficially set a record daily average wind speed of \n24.4 mph. High Wind Warning in effect until 5 am as models \nsuggest winds weakening below criteria. I'm not so sure. Will \ncontinue to monitor over the next several hours in case I have \nto extend the Warning a few more hours. Otherwise Wind Advisory \nmost areas until 2 pm today.\n\nThe other story today into Sunday will be precipitation chances\nassociated with the upper low off northern Baja this morning.\nThis upper low continues to pull in moisture from the south\nwith regional radars this morning showing scattered south across\nwestern Pima county west through Yuma county and south into the\nnorthern Gulf of CA. Scattered showers will remain across wrn\nhalf of Pima county until this afternoon before expanding east\nlate this afternoon into this evening as the upper low starts to\nlift NE toward AZ. Can't rule out an isolated thunderstorms.\nRainfall totals this weekend mostly less than 0.25\".\n\nA slow moving Pacific upper level trof will keep unsettled \nconditions next week with daily chances of showers (20-50 \npercent) each day. Daily high temperatures will remain below \nnormal for much of the next 7 days.",
